  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1408.07 Used Oil Management",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1408.07 Used Oil Management. A used oil processor/re-refiner shall comply with the requirements of Env-Hw 1405.03 and shall equip containers and tanks used to store or process used oil with a secondary containment system that:\n\n(a) Is impervious to used oil to prevent any used oil released into the containment system from migrating out of the system to the soil, groundwater, or surface water;\n\n(b) Is capable of holding:\n\n(1) For container storage, 110% of the volume of the largest container in the storage area or 10% of the total volume of containers, whichever is greater; or\n\n(2) For tank storage, 110% of the volume of the largest tank within the storage area; and\n\n(c) Consists of:\n\n(1) A combination of dikes, berms, or retaining walls with a floor that covers the entire area within the dikes, berms, or retaining walls, except that the floor need not cover where an existing tank or portions thereof meet(s) the ground; or\n\n(2) An equivalent secondary containment system, such as a double-walled tank with a fill gauge and high-level alarm.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
